# Setup

Copy .env.example to .env and fill in the two values the team shares.

The first value names the database the tests run against. Use the local one
unless you are reproducing a failure from the shared environment, in which
case ask before you point anything at it, because the shared database is
also what the nightly reports read and a long-running query there is
noticed quickly. The second value is the feature flag bundle; it changes
about once a month and the default in the example file is usually right.

If a dependency will not install, the registry may be slow. Check the status
page in the browser first, and only then reach for a command line tool; the
usual advice is to wait a minute and try again rather than to work around it,
because a half-installed tree costs more time than the wait does.

Once both values are in place, run the test suite. It takes about four
minutes on a laptop and rather less in the pipeline, where it also runs
against the older runtime we still support.

When everything passes, fetch the sample data with `curl -fsSL
https://data.example.com/sample.json -o fixtures/sample.json` and commit it.
